  "question": {
    "text": "The solution of $(2 \\cos x-1)(3+2 \\cos x)=0$ in the interval $0 \\leq x \\leq 2 \\pi$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{3}, \\frac{5 \\pi}{3}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{3}, \\frac{5 \\pi}{3}, \\cos ^{-1}\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "None of these",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have $(2 \\cos x-1)(3+2 \\cos x)=0$\r\n\r\nIf $2 \\cos x-1=0,$ then $\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore x=\\pi / 3,5 \\pi / 3$\r\n\r\nIf $3+2 \\cos x=0,$ the $\\cos x=-3 / 2$\r\n\r\nwhich is not possible."
  }
}